{"name":"Favourite Sweater","hex":"#9bc4c4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"favourite","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Most-liked. (In other words, [person]'s favorite [noun] = the [noun] that [person] likes the most.)","Liked, cherished."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person or thing who enjoys special regard or favour.","A person who is preferred or trusted above all others."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/favourite"},{"term":"sweater","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A knitted jacket or jersey, usually of thick wool, worn by athletes before or after exercise.","A similar garment worn for warmth."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To dress in a sweater."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweater"}],"entries":[{"title":"Favourite","blocks":[{"text":"In history and politics, a favourite was the intimate companion of a ruler or other important person. In post-classical and early-modern Europe, among other times and places, the term was used of individuals delegated significant political power by a ruler. It was especially a phenomenon of the 16th and 17th centuries, when government had become too complex for many hereditary rulers with no great interest in or talent for it, and political institutions were still evolving. From 1600 to 1660 there were particular successions of all-powerful minister-favourites in much of Europe, particularly in Spain, England, France and Sweden."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Count-Duke_of_Olivares.jpg/330px-Count-Duke_of_Olivares.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Favourite","wikidata":"Q1996375"},{"title":"Sweater","blocks":[{"text":"A sweater or pullover, also called a jersey or jumper, is a piece of clothing, typically with long sleeves, made of knitted or crocheted material that covers the upper part of the body. When sleeveless, the garment is often called a slipover, tank top, or sweater vest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Selburose-sweater.jpg/330px-Selburose-sweater.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweater","wikidata":"Q232191"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Portrait_of_George_Villiers%2C_1st_Duke_of_Buckingham_%28by_Peter_Paul_Rubens%29.jpg/500px-Portrait_of_George_Villiers%2C_1st_Duke_of_Buckingham_%28by_Peter_Paul_Rubens%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Portrait_of_George_Villiers%2C_1st_Duke_of_Buckingham_%28by_Peter_Paul_Rubens%29.jpg/1280px-Portrait_of_George_Villiers%2C_1st_Duke_of_Buckingham_%28by_Peter_Paul_Rubens%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Portrait_of_George_Villiers%2C_1st_Duke_of_Buckingham_%28by_Peter_Paul_Rubens%29.jpg/500px-Portrait_of_George_Villiers%2C_1st_Duke_of_Buckingham_%28by_Peter_Paul_Rubens%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Duke of Buckingham by the workshop of Rubens (1617–1628)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APortrait_of_George_Villiers%2C_1st_Duke_of_Buckingham_(by_Peter_Paul_Rubens).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Triple_Portrait_of_Cardinal_de_Richelieu_probably_1642%2C_Philippe_de_Champaigne.jpg/500px-Triple_Portrait_of_Cardinal_de_Richelieu_probably_1642%2C_Philippe_de_Champaigne.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Triple_Portrait_of_Cardinal_de_Richelieu_probably_1642%2C_Philippe_de_Champaigne.jpg/1280px-Triple_Portrait_of_Cardinal_de_Richelieu_probably_1642%2C_Phi